       <div class="field field-name--body field-type--text-with-summary field-label--hidden field-formatter--text-default">
      <h2>Mission</h2>
<p>The Prince George's County Board of Elections seeks to promote voter education, administer an efficient voting process, maintain an accurate voter registration database, and ensure that elected officials are elected in accordance with Federal, State, and County election laws.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Prince George's County Board of Elections is Seeking Fluent Spanish Speaking Interpreters to Serve in Our polling Precincts on Nov. 3rd. Please Click the Link Below for Details or Call 301.341.7353</h4>
<p><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/Spanish%20Speaking%20Recruitment%20Flyer%20-%20Copy.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="53c87907-1da1-4640-b73e-0434df36dbba" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Spanish Speaking Recruitment">Spanish Interpreters Flyer</a></p>
<h2>Responsibilities</h2>
<p>The Board of Elections is responsible for supervising elections, voter registration, and record keeping, and the administration of election laws in Prince George's County in accordance with the <a href="https://elections.maryland.gov/laws_and_regs/election_law.html">Election Law Article of the Annotated Code of Maryland</a>. The Board and the Election Administrator seek to provide voter registration to every County citizen who wants it.</p>
<h3>Track Your Mail-In Ballot!</h3>
<p><strong>MPWR </strong>service provides insight into the status of mail-in ballots processed through the State vendor Taylor and then through the USPS system. Click the link below.</p>
<p><a class="coh-style-button-one" href="https://mpwrelection.com/maryland/voter">Track Your Mail-In Ballot with MPWR</a></p>
<p><strong>Please Note:&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p><strong>MPWR </strong>cannot provide any details about&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="eb95e3a1a0db1b7e6709c51c0e1ea583b">1) web-delivery ballots.</li>
<li data-list-item-id="ef9924cafa0a58e55f79b7c2059568a71">2) ballots in any overseas postal system.</li>
<li data-list-item-id="ee6b255e24bd5c92baa374331acc73e26">3) voted ballots that are returned through drop boxes.</li>
</ul>
<p style="line-height:normal;"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12.0pt;"></span></p>
<h3>2026 Gubernatorial Election</h3>
<p><strong>The Specimen Ballot is available below. If you have any concerns about any of the ballot questions listed, please contact the Office of Law at </strong><a href="mailto:legislative-ool@co.pg.md.us"><strong>legislative-ool@co.pg.md.us</strong></a></p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="ee57e41a575460d70488ffa6e192fd25f"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/Specimen%20Ballot%20-%20English%20Version.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="341a0412-d171-44fe-8188-cee78d618002" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Specimen Ballot 2026 - English Version">Specimen Ballot-English Version</a></li>
<li data-list-item-id="e40b91cd042ed532586d08ab4c9a36c7b"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/Specimen%20Ballot%20-%20Spanish%20Version.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="d712691e-e334-41c3-9f86-6e4d6efdd659" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Specimen Ballot 2026 - Spanish Version">Specimen Ballot - Spanish Version</a></li>
<li data-list-item-id="edd08f6925a653da55e33e8553255051e"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/CF%20006%202026%20GUB%20PRIMARY%205.19.26.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="900a577f-4de1-44ed-814b-ba787621eb6b" data-entity-substitution="media" title="CF 006 GUB Primary 5.19.26">Filed Candidates</a></li>
<li data-list-item-id="efbfcb3e821fb8ff02456f1f95863dcf1"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/Updated%20Ballot%20942026.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="122a8bae-867c-4ce6-8c6c-06f7d6f5ec92" data-entity-substitution="media" title="2026 GG26 Ballot ">2026 Gubernatorial General Ballot</a></li>
<li data-list-item-id="e76a904556a2d881c9eea767e028be0c3"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/GP26%20%20Updated%20Ballot%20Questions.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="f91f53fd-2dad-4336-a703-b698e1d1df78" data-entity-substitution="media" title="2026 GG Ballot Questions">2026 Ballot Questions&nbsp;</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Canvassing:</h3>
<p>Prince George’s County Board of Elections will begin "early canvassing" of the ballots for the 2026&nbsp;<br>Gubernatorial General Election:&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="e395dfce6c3e429ed15bef660de7e7abf">Date: October 13 - 20, 2026.</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e445c96d576d713f848b5e57dce73d4a1">Hours: 9:00am to 5:30pm.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Post-Election Canvassing:</h3>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="ef4b67361c6b07f94eec1c31de76ef395">Date: November 5, 2026 - until completed.</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e41b5b69a65f2422edb5bf931eac3e5a1">Hours for post-election canvassing will be as follows: &nbsp;10:00am – 5:30pm; each<br>day after the times will be 9:00am – 5:30pm.</li>
</ul>
<h3>&nbsp;Provisional Canvassing:</h3>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="e3b32152b183b6d3e76dad11b0986480e">Date: November 11, 2026&nbsp;</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e21e43b839651b5e694da61671d35fc60">Hours: 10:00am</li>
</ul>
<p>The general public will be able to observe the process. Canvassing will be conducted at the following location:</p>
<p>&nbsp;Prince George’s County Board of Elections&nbsp;<br>1100 Mercantile Lane, Suite 135<br>&nbsp;Largo, MD 20774</p>
<h3>Primary Election Results</h3>
<p><strong>Early Voting </strong>- June 11, 2026 through June 18, 2026 (7am - 8pm)<br><strong>Election Day</strong> - June 23, 2026 - 7am - 8pm</p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="ee55e8149c1b3d2c8fd398b5290d0482c"><a href="https://elections.maryland.gov/elections/2026/Primary_results/gen_results_2026_by_county_17.html">Primary Election Results</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>General Election</h3>
<p><strong>Early Voting</strong> - October 22, 2026 through October 29, 2026 (7am - 8pm)<br><strong>Election Day</strong> - November 3, 2026 - 7am - 8pm</p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="edc86bc6f8db445a518c0fc404cf859d9"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/DROP%20BOX%20LOCATONS%20-%20Updated%209-9-2026%20-%20%202026%20Gubernatorial_0.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="72daf22f-1563-4ddb-8d9e-2af20ee8c2ce" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Prince George's County Board of Elections 2026 GUBERNATORIAL GENERAL ELECTION Drop Box Locations">2026 Drop Box Locations</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Your Voter Information</h3>
<p>Use the&nbsp;<a href="https://voterservices.elections.maryland.gov/VoterSearch">Maryland State Board of Elections Voter Lookup</a>&nbsp;tool to find your current voter registration and district information.</p>
<p><a class="coh-style-button-one" href="https://voterservices.elections.maryland.gov/VoterSearch">Check Your Voter Registration</a></p>
<h3>Current County Districts, Precincts, and Polling Places</h3>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="eb295bb942004ee5847071a0788b5a7d2"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/2026%20Polling%20Place%20Changes.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="a20327f2-7ca3-4bed-bb49-18f74bd7c11a" data-entity-substitution="media" title="2026 Polling Place Changes">2026 Polling Place Changes</a></li>
<li data-list-item-id="efda6109aaaea55f7e455223553e9109b"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/2026%20-%20District-Precincts%20-%20327%20-%20Updated_0.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="59639158-81d0-40f2-b076-3e34c88b26e3" data-entity-substitution="media" title="2026-District-Precincts-327">District - Precincts - 2026</a></li>
<li data-list-item-id="e7c40395b89da30a16eaacf8927eebc19"><a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/2026%20Early%20Voting%20Sites%20-13%20sites.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="33eff6ce-bf2d-47b1-9770-ce9c2062c2b4" data-entity-substitution="media" title="2026 Early Voting Sites - 13 sites">2026 Early Voting Sites</a></li>
</ul>
<p>The Prince George's County Board of Elections wants to ensure that all eligible voters in our county can access the polls fairly and equally. To support this effort, we keep a contact list of people and organizations who want to know when Local Board Meetings will discuss changes to polling place locations.</p>
<p><strong>If you want to receive notifications about attending these meetings, please complete the Polling Place Change Notification Form.</strong></p>
<p><a class="coh-style-button-one" href="https://app.smartsheet.com/b/form/89bc59f8f57e4bc7a878014dfc015281">Polling Place Change Notification Form</a></p>
<h3>Board of Elections Meetings</h3>
<p>The next <a href="/sites/default/files/media-document/Board%20Meeting%20Agenda%201132026.pdf" data-entity-type="media" data-entity-uuid="b5c9f2f2-9e44-414c-9616-95da9e811592" data-entity-substitution="media" title="Board Meeting Agenda 1132026">board meeting </a>will be conducted (virtual) on Tuesday, November 3rd, 2026, at 8:30 pm.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Prince George's County Board of Elections&nbsp;<br>1100 Mercantile Lane, Suite 115A<br>Largo, MD 20774</p>
<h3>Agendas &amp; Minutes</h3>
<p>Agendas are available before the meetings. Minutes are available after approval.</p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="e10c74c9aca115a5f4c466bf9c1dbfe5f"><a href="https://www.princegeorgescountymd.gov/government/county-government/agendas-minutes?year=&amp;field_event_start_value_1=&amp;field_event_end_value=&amp;field_boards_commissions_target_id_1=466#center-3090678413">View All Agendas and Minutes</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Board Meeting Videos</h3>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="ea981086172d713c51a91bfb886bcaac2"><a href="https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meetup-join/19%3ameeting_NTI5YmU3MGItOTAwZS00ZDdkLTkxMGUtOTEzZjcwMDFmNDg1%40thread.v2/0?context=%7b%22Tid%22%3a%224146bdda-ddc1-4d2a-a1b2-1a64cc3c837b%22%2c%22Oid%22%3a%229fcc06a3-c30e-4fc0-b5f9-3d44fc23e0c4%22%7d">Link to join current board meeting livestream via Microsoft Teams</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Beginning in June 2025, board meetings will be livestreamed, and videos of the board meetings will be made available for review on our YouTube channel. Videos of board meetings will be posted and published as soon as possible.</p>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="ef9e9e5c4d4c49ddb0179ca0d8ab91193"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLi6YomQwclK0k9cHQSIQm6nBsqePDrPaq">View All Board Meeting Videos</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Board Members</h3>
<p>The Governor, by and with the consent of the Senate, appoints five people who constitute the Board of Elections. The appointees are selected from lists provided by the County Central Committee of the Democratic and Republican parties. The Board is responsible for the supervision of all County, State, and Federal Elections held in Prince George's County.</p>
<h3>Members</h3>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="e4223baa78840bdfd6cdf0bb8ebac799c">Beatrice P. Tignor (D), President</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e632587cdf6acb6963847a1379f12fbbe">Roberta B. Deegan (R), Vice President</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e0b228301d15169f4a695e4aa9164646f">Faye M. Howell (D)</li>
<li data-list-item-id="ecdbab28b28f5d60f7f40746863a17c4f">Carletta L. Lundy (D)</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e997ee94d032d9370819cc482259e5192">Terri L. Williams (D)&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h3>Substitute Members</h3>
<ul>
<li data-list-item-id="e2a1691d1da925529a4f72561d8036e23">Michael M. Gorman. (R) &nbsp;</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e02845f23edd67f4bacba207fa550da86">Alethea Smalls (D) &nbsp;</li>
<li data-list-item-id="e4abf6abeab132ba4f8a86abd10a901d8">LaVerne Poteat Scott (D)</li>
</ul>
<h3>Election Administrator</h3>
<p>Wendy Honesty-Bey</p>
<p><a href="tel:301-341-7300">301-341-7300</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
        </div>
